{
  "core_message": "A 1898 novella eerily predicted the Titanic disaster fourteen years later.",
  "mood": "curious",
  "title": "13 survivors from an 1898 ship that predicted Titanic",
  "description": "Morgan Robertson’s novel *Futility* described a fictional liner, the Titan, that sank after striking an iceberg in 1898. Fourteen years later, the real Titanic met the same fate, sparking speculation of prophetic foresight.\n\nKey points:\n• 1898 novel warned of an iceberg collision and insufficient lifeboats.\n• Only thirteen survivors were reported.\n• The book was reissued after Titanic’s wreck, highlighting uncanny parallels.\n\nBased on the Wikipedia article \"The Wreck of the Titan: Or, Futility\" (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Wreck_of_the_Titan:_Or,_Futility), licensed CC BY-SA 4.0.\n\nImages from Wikimedia Commons:\nFutility Original First Edition Cover.jpg (Unknown author Unknown author, Public domain): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Futility_Original_First_Edition_Cover.jpg\nFutility by Morgan Robertson - cover.png (Morgan Robertson, Public domain): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Futility_by_Morgan_Robertson_-_cover.png\nFutility Original First Edition Cover.jpg (Unknown author Unknown author, Public domain): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Futility_Original_First_Edition_Cover.jpg",
